# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .trivyignore — documented acceptances for the container image scanner.
#
# Format: one CVE id per line. Comments require "# " prefix; trivy treats
# any non-CVE line as ignored.
#
# DO NOT add a CVE here without:
#   1. A reference to the upstream issue / advisory
#   2. The reason this is acceptable (e.g. unreachable code path,
#      vendor pinned, fix not yet available)
#   3. The plan to remove the entry (e.g. "after Next.js 15 upgrade")
#
# Review this file every release cut. Stale entries hide live threats.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ─── docbrain-web (next/dist/compiled bundled deps) ──────────────────────────
# These CVEs live inside the next.js *compiled* output — Next ships its own
# bundled copies of cross-spawn / glob / minimatch / tar / postcss / lodash
# at publish time. npm overrides have no effect on them; only a Next.js
# bump can resolve them.
#
# Plan: bump next 14.2.35 → 15.x in a dedicated PR (requires app-router /
# react 18→19 compat review). Tracked separately.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# cross-spawn ReDoS — bundled inside next/dist/compiled/
# https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-3xgq-45jj-v275
CVE-2024-21538

# glob command injection — bundled inside next/dist/compiled/
# https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4mwc-9ph6-x4vp
CVE-2025-64756

